1
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:21,390
you stop?

2
00:00:29,660 --> 00:00:30,900
Shout It Up.

3
00:00:58,712 --> 00:01:00,160
Let's go! Welcome!

4
00:01:04,140 --> 00:01:05,377
Dreaming On! My

5
00:01:05,460 --> 00:01:12,460
dream...

6
00:01:19,460 --> 00:01:21,460
Dreaming of.

7
00:01:23,460 --> 00:01:24,290
Woah!

8
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:26,290
Woah!

9
00:01:26,373 --> 00:01:27,203
Woah!

10
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:39,940
Hey, Buggy!

11
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:41,080
Guess who's back?

12
00:01:41,340 --> 00:01:42,820
Captain Roger's here!

13
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:44,080
Captain Roger?

14
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:52,400
It's really them!

15
00:01:53,660 --> 00:01:56,280
And what a flashy entrance, too!

16
00:01:57,720 --> 00:01:58,550
Yeah!

17
00:01:58,633 --> 00:01:59,820
It's Roger!

18
00:02:22,060 --> 00:02:24,480
When Roger returned from Laugh Tale,

19
00:02:24,820 --> 00:02:27,585
Red Taro greeted him
gleefully with a question,

20
00:02:27,740 --> 00:02:30,328
only to break down into
tears moments later.

21
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:41,660
The birth of the King of the Pirates
caused quite a commotion around the world,

22
00:02:42,140 --> 00:02:44,846
which prompted the Navy
to react aggressively.

23
00:02:45,460 --> 00:02:48,577
The man who achieved
wealth, fame, and power.

24
00:02:48,660 --> 00:02:51,397
That calls you a legend of our time.

25
00:02:51,480 --> 00:02:54,860
The King of the Pirates, Gold Roger.

26
00:02:57,440 --> 00:02:59,320
Except it's Gold D.

27
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:03,837
Roger Although, being called
King of the Pirates ain't so bad.

28
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:07,557
It's no wonder the world government
wants to cover up your name.

29
00:03:07,640 --> 00:03:10,346
You've really earned
that reputation of yours.

30
00:03:11,780 --> 00:03:16,097
The world had a name for everything
that Roger gained on the final island.

31
00:03:16,180 --> 00:03:21,157
They called it the legendary
treasure one piece;

32
00:03:21,240 --> 00:03:27,017
they have no idea you do realize
that because of your fame,

33
00:03:27,100 --> 00:03:29,637
everyone is going to be
out to get you, right?

34
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:35,640
We'll take down Roger! ARGH!

35
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:45,440
Find him at all costs!

36
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:47,856
Let's nap his treasure for ourselves!

37
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:51,296
They say he's got everything
tucked away in his stash!

38
00:04:06,700 --> 00:04:09,582
Looking back now, it's
been a miraculous journey.

39
00:04:09,760 --> 00:04:14,289
Hard to believe how far we made it,
especially with my short life expectancy.

40
00:04:15,820 --> 00:04:18,280
I have nothing but gratitude to you all.

41
00:04:21,140 --> 00:04:22,880
Whoa, whoa! Come on, now!

42
00:04:23,100 --> 00:04:24,617
Where is this jump coming from?

43
00:04:24,700 --> 00:04:26,317
You can't lay it on this thick!

44
00:04:26,400 --> 00:04:27,977
Don't make me blush, Captain.

45
00:04:28,060 --> 00:04:28,900
You rascal!

46
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:42,860
Then I'll come out and
say it. We're ready.

47
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:44,800
Just lay it on us.

48
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:57,960
I am hereby disbanding the Roger Pirates.

49
00:05:21,300 --> 00:05:23,617
The birth is at hand.

50
00:05:23,700 --> 00:05:26,617
Our sovereign shall soon be born.

51
00:05:26,700 --> 00:05:29,257
And another in a distant sea.

52
00:05:29,340 --> 00:05:32,757
And in time the two rulers shall meet.

53
00:05:32,840 --> 00:05:35,400
A joy that even the whales sing of.

54
00:05:39,320 --> 00:05:43,000
We have waited for this
day for far too long.

55
00:05:44,060 --> 00:05:45,640
It's nearly here.

56
00:05:45,880 --> 00:05:48,640
And surely all shall go well this time.

57
00:05:48,900 --> 00:05:51,080
Only ten until the birth.

58
00:05:51,700 --> 00:05:53,820
Then another fifteen to grow.

59
00:05:55,200 --> 00:05:57,020
Who are you?

60
00:05:57,360 --> 00:06:01,020
How are you able to talk so
loudly all the way down here?

61
00:06:04,020 --> 00:06:07,800
So, Charlie, when will this
mermaid princess be born?

62
00:06:08,120 --> 00:06:09,000
This many!

63
00:06:13,380 --> 00:06:15,080
About that voice...

64
00:06:15,760 --> 00:06:16,820
You heard it?

65
00:06:17,540 --> 00:06:19,620
I'm certain it's telling the truth.

66
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:25,420
Soon a great person will be born,
and one day, it'll even surpass us.

67
00:06:30,920 --> 00:06:33,397
Perhaps we were a bit before our time.

68
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:37,460
I do wonder who will find
the one piece in the end?

69
00:06:38,900 --> 00:06:41,297
That would be my son, obviously.

70
00:06:41,380 --> 00:06:43,117
You don't have one.

71
00:06:43,200 --> 00:06:46,080
Not yet, but I may have one in the future.

72
00:06:50,020 --> 00:06:52,357
All right, time to drink.

73
00:06:52,440 --> 00:06:54,977
Head us toward some place with no navy.

74
00:06:55,060 --> 00:06:57,840
I'm gonna get off the ship first! Yeah!

75
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:05,880
Now, listen up!

76
00:07:06,060 --> 00:07:08,980
Be sure that Odin makes
it home safely after me!

77
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:19,440
By the way, Odin, I plan to meet with
Whitebeard once more before I keel over.

78
00:07:20,860 --> 00:07:23,684
Should I have him send
Izo back to Bono as well?

79
00:07:24,380 --> 00:07:25,210
Nope.

80
00:07:26,220 --> 00:07:28,840
He's gotten quite
comfortable on that ship.

81
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:33,626
I promise you'll tell him to
take care of White Kashi for me.

82
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:35,320
All right, will do.

83
00:07:44,140 --> 00:07:46,440
Roger had a few words with Rayleigh.

84
00:07:46,980 --> 00:07:51,360
A man known as the Dark King was
his oldest friend in Confidant.

85
00:07:57,760 --> 00:08:00,080
Then Roger disembarked.

86
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:05,908
The ship's doctor Crocus sent him off
with a bundle of medicine for treatment.

87
00:08:06,720 --> 00:08:09,660
His disease was in its final stages.

88
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:12,820
This was a man's farewell.

89
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:16,988
Not a single tear was shed as
we were filled with solemnness.

90
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:22,097
Crying wouldn't befit the
king of pirates' crew.

91
00:08:22,180 --> 00:08:24,600
So we stood.

92
00:08:25,140 --> 00:08:26,640
Utterly stoic.

93
00:08:36,660 --> 00:08:38,340
This is unbelievable.

94
00:08:39,640 --> 00:08:42,460
And look at all those
wrecked ships over there.

95
00:08:43,180 --> 00:08:44,440
As expected.

96
00:08:44,940 --> 00:08:47,587
This next part will be
difficult to maneuver.

97
00:08:47,740 --> 00:08:51,505
One wrong turn into a current and
your vessel will be in pieces.

98
00:08:52,180 --> 00:08:56,437
Until this point, we had no reason to
close the country, but that has changed.

99
00:08:56,520 --> 00:09:01,020
We must open its ports to the
world before Joy Boy comes.

100
00:09:04,920 --> 00:09:08,640
You all better take care of
yourselves until next time.

101
00:09:11,900 --> 00:09:14,257
It's not as though I was
the one who was dying,

102
00:09:14,340 --> 00:09:17,420
so we parted ways with
smiles on our faces.

103
00:09:18,140 --> 00:09:20,493
We all knew we would meet again one day.

104
00:09:30,280 --> 00:09:31,520
My dear!

105
00:09:32,420 --> 00:09:34,340
My beloved wife!

106
00:09:34,560 --> 00:09:36,560
I've waited so long for this day!

107
00:09:36,980 --> 00:09:37,940
Hiyori goes!

108
00:09:40,960 --> 00:09:41,800
Chaka!

109
00:09:42,980 --> 00:09:43,820
Momonosuke!

110
00:09:44,540 --> 00:09:45,380
Hiyori!

111
00:09:46,520 --> 00:09:48,320
I missed you two!

112
00:09:49,020 --> 00:09:49,860
Terribly!

113
00:09:53,420 --> 00:09:57,557
I go out to sea for a bit, and as soon
as I come home, you're all grown up!

114
00:09:57,640 --> 00:09:58,470
Yes!

115
00:09:58,553 --> 00:10:00,927
I hope all has been well
while you were away!

116
00:10:02,920 --> 00:10:05,260
My boy has proper manners, too!

117
00:10:08,240 --> 00:10:10,064
Good to have you back, my lord.

118
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:13,160
You jackass!

119
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:16,577
Is that how you properly
address your lord?!

120
00:10:16,660 --> 00:10:19,800
I was unaware that you were
deserving of such things.

121
00:10:26,240 --> 00:10:28,277
It's so nice to see you.

122
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:30,677
Lord Odin, welcome back!

123
00:10:30,760 --> 00:10:32,060
How was your trip?

124
00:10:32,580 --> 00:10:34,380
Otoki, how wonderful!

125
00:10:40,720 --> 00:10:43,857
I didn't expect that
I'd still be so popular.

126
00:10:43,940 --> 00:10:46,817
I neglected our country
for quite some time.

127
00:10:46,900 --> 00:10:48,937
I thought they'd be angrier.

128
00:10:49,020 --> 00:10:50,757
Thank your wife!

129
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:53,040
This is the result of Lady Toki.

130
00:10:53,260 --> 00:10:57,040
She is a woman of great
character, truly beloved by all.

131
00:10:57,340 --> 00:11:01,317
Every day she would devote herself fully
to helping citizens around the town.

132
00:11:01,400 --> 00:11:05,720
She toiled and sweated by their side,
and told tales of your triumphs,

133
00:11:05,820 --> 00:11:08,377
but never acted haughty
because of her stature.

134
00:11:08,460 --> 00:11:10,537
No surprise the Lady Toki's beloved,

135
00:11:10,620 --> 00:11:13,497
and the people here are quite
fond of your children as well.

136
00:11:13,580 --> 00:11:17,797
Even in your absence, they have spoken
nothing but praise for you as well.

137
00:11:17,880 --> 00:11:19,137
And that's not all.

138
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:23,937
The number of people who had ill will
towards Jugarra has dwindled down to nothing.

139
00:11:24,020 --> 00:11:24,850
Incredible.

140
00:11:25,020 --> 00:11:26,196
You're all too kind.

141
00:11:26,440 --> 00:11:27,320
My thanks.

142
00:11:27,860 --> 00:11:29,217
Please don't mention it.

143
00:11:29,300 --> 00:11:31,097
We did it out of our love for you.

144
00:11:31,180 --> 00:11:32,010
Right, kids?

145
00:11:33,620 --> 00:11:34,460
I'm jealous!

146
00:11:34,760 --> 00:11:36,460
I wish the ladies liked me!

147
00:11:39,520 --> 00:11:40,400
Hey, Kiku.

148
00:11:40,620 --> 00:11:42,340
I have some news about Izo.

149
00:11:43,340 --> 00:11:45,237
I already heard it all
from Doggy and Kitty.

150
00:11:45,320 --> 00:11:46,560
I'm glad he's well.

151
00:11:47,240 --> 00:11:48,070
Great.

152
00:11:48,300 --> 00:11:51,620
Tell me, what has become
of Denjiro and Ashura?

153
00:11:51,940 --> 00:11:54,220
I didn't see them last year, either.

154
00:11:54,760 --> 00:11:57,397
Ashura became the boss of
the Yakuza and Mountain

155
00:11:57,480 --> 00:12:00,480
Bandits and Kuri to make
sure they don't misbehave.

156
00:12:00,920 --> 00:12:04,057
Denjiro, on the other hand, has
been wandering all over Wano,

157
00:12:04,140 --> 00:12:06,022
borrowing and paying back money.

158
00:12:07,400 --> 00:12:10,017
Neither of those lifestyles
sound very comfortable,

159
00:12:10,100 --> 00:12:12,512
or like they belong in a thriving nation.

160
00:12:13,160 --> 00:12:13,990
Indeed.

161
00:12:14,360 --> 00:12:18,419
There is another reason that everyone
is overjoyed about your return.

162
00:12:19,700 --> 00:12:22,347
I will tell you the
story from the beginning.

163
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:26,897
After you left, we did our best to run
Kaido in the absence of its daimyo.

164
00:12:26,980 --> 00:12:31,509
However, it was no easy task, even with
the help of the citizens at our side.

165
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:32,640
I thank you.

166
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:34,193
It must have been hard.

167
00:12:34,400 --> 00:12:36,540
Tell me, how is my father faring?

168
00:12:42,680 --> 00:12:45,020
I have some unfortunate news. I see.

169
00:12:47,400 --> 00:12:50,694
That would mean he really was
in poor health, I suppose.

170
00:12:53,140 --> 00:12:54,060
What a shame.

171
00:12:54,340 --> 00:12:56,977
I wish I'd been there
for him on his deathbed.

172
00:12:57,060 --> 00:13:00,236
There's a conundrum concerning
the Shogun's successor.

173
00:13:00,380 --> 00:13:04,440
Before passing, Lord Tsukiyaki
made a request that was quite odd.

174
00:13:04,680 --> 00:13:05,960
It involves Odoji.

175
00:13:07,760 --> 00:13:09,160
Please let me money.

176
00:13:11,520 --> 00:13:14,397
The more I heard, the more confused I was.

177
00:13:14,480 --> 00:13:17,497
Suddenly, Orochi was like a brother to me.

178
00:13:17,580 --> 00:13:20,797
All I did was lend him money
out of respect to Yasuie;

179
00:13:20,880 --> 00:13:23,237
that man never once
returned a single coin.

180
00:13:23,320 --> 00:13:24,150
Of it,

181
00:13:24,233 --> 00:13:27,597
either I also learned that
Orochi is a descendant of the

182
00:13:27,680 --> 00:13:30,837
Kurozumi clan that caused a
terrible incident in the past,

183
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:34,437
so it was even more shocking to
hear that he was occupying the.

184
00:13:34,520 --> 00:13:36,840
position of shogun as my proxy.

185
00:13:37,160 --> 00:13:38,866
Did you notice the factories?

186
00:13:39,100 --> 00:13:40,924
You must have on your way here.

187
00:13:41,100 --> 00:13:43,517
Each is filled with men
who oversee the labor.

188
00:13:43,600 --> 00:13:46,417
They're clear evidence our
country has changed for the worse.

189
00:13:46,500 --> 00:13:49,417
In every region, the workers
are forced to slave away.

190
00:13:49,500 --> 00:13:53,676
Their wages are far too meager to
survive on, all thanks to the shogun.

191
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:55,160
But how can this be?

192
00:13:55,480 --> 00:13:58,957
Why is the whole country obeying
orders from a lowlife like Orochi?

193
00:13:59,040 --> 00:13:59,870
It's simple.

194
00:13:59,980 --> 00:14:03,156
He has the support of a
despicable pirate named Kaido.

195
00:14:03,280 --> 00:14:05,757
He's a beast in strength
and character alike.

196
00:14:05,840 --> 00:14:09,600
Kaido's the reason why Orochi
can do as he pleases. It's true.

197
00:14:09,840 --> 00:14:12,577
There was one time we tried to
take a step - Not another word,

198
00:14:12,660 --> 00:14:13,490
Kin'emon.

199
00:14:13,573 --> 00:14:17,220
Leave it at that. Tell
me. What is it? Speak up!

200
00:14:18,680 --> 00:14:19,510
Raizo,

201
00:14:19,780 --> 00:14:21,997
Take Lord Momonosuke and Lady Hyori.

202
00:14:22,080 --> 00:14:23,021
out of the room.

203
00:14:23,120 --> 00:14:23,950
Sir,

204
00:14:24,033 --> 00:14:24,863
pardon.

205
00:14:26,880 --> 00:14:29,757
This incident took place
about a half a year ago.

206
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:34,880
There was a man who refused to work
at a weapons factory and, well...

207
00:14:36,080 --> 00:14:37,760
His family was murdered.

208
00:14:39,380 --> 00:14:43,600
We felt we could no longer stay
passive in the face of such cruelty.

209
00:14:44,080 --> 00:14:46,960
With fury in our hearts
and swords in our hands,

210
00:14:47,080 --> 00:14:49,845
we marched to the capital
to end Orochi's rule.

211
00:14:51,180 --> 00:14:55,827
However we were thwarted, Kaido's
subordinates snuck into Kuri right behind us.

212
00:14:56,620 --> 00:14:58,540
They infiltrated the castle.

213
00:15:01,520 --> 00:15:04,873
Then those rogues threatened
the life of Lord Momonosuke,

214
00:15:05,080 --> 00:15:06,980
future heir of the Kozuki clan

215
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:15,520
Forgive me

216
00:15:17,620 --> 00:15:21,561
In the end, the enemies were driven
back by Kawamatsu and Dogstorm,

217
00:15:21,800 --> 00:15:24,212
who had been standing guard at the castle

218
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:33,200
However, it was Lady Toki who
truly saved your son's life

219
00:15:34,380 --> 00:15:37,940
She used her own body to
shield him from a deadly arrow

220
00:15:39,520 --> 00:15:43,960
My sincerest apologies Because
of our reckless actions,

221
00:15:44,300 --> 00:15:47,497
she suffered a terrible leg
injury We put your family's

222
00:15:47,580 --> 00:15:51,500
lives at risk without
thinking first I'm so sorry,

223
00:15:51,660 --> 00:15:53,820
Lord Odin This is unforgivable

224
00:15:55,800 --> 00:15:56,860
Please, show me.

225
00:15:57,160 --> 00:15:58,400
Odin, I'm fine.

226
00:15:58,880 --> 00:16:00,586
The wound has already healed.

227
00:16:07,720 --> 00:16:09,100
Thank you, Toki.

228
00:16:09,480 --> 00:16:11,040
You saved our child.

229
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:15,120
It must have hurt.

230
00:16:17,140 --> 00:16:18,820
You can't lash out.

231
00:16:18,980 --> 00:16:22,745
I don't want to invite another
attack over something so trivial.

232
00:16:23,820 --> 00:16:27,920
You, you, you call this trivial?

233
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:34,380
Listen, Toki, I can handle this myself.

234
00:16:34,960 --> 00:16:37,000
You don't know of my past.

235
00:16:39,060 --> 00:16:41,960
I see now how Orochi does things.

236
00:16:43,260 --> 00:16:46,180
Retainers, stay here and guard my family.

237
00:16:48,380 --> 00:16:49,840
Please, Odin.

238
00:16:52,820 --> 00:16:55,040
You must protect Karoo!

239
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:04,700
While I'm not exactly keen on politics,

240
00:17:05,240 --> 00:17:08,077
I think it's clear what
happened while I was away.

241
00:17:08,160 --> 00:17:10,640
A fool has taken control of Wano.

242
00:17:11,160 --> 00:17:16,437
A weak, cowardly little vermin hid
behind the strength of a fearsome pirate.

243
00:17:16,520 --> 00:17:20,220
and took advantage of a country
where no one could intervene.

244
00:17:25,680 --> 00:17:27,800
I see what he has done.

245
00:17:28,580 --> 00:17:31,640
He's turned this land into a hellscape!

246
00:17:53,140 --> 00:17:54,800
Oh Call backup, huh?

247
00:17:55,980 --> 00:17:58,857
Come in Kozuki Oden is on his way to the

248
00:17:58,940 --> 00:18:02,360
flower capital report to
Shogun Orochi right now

249
00:18:14,520 --> 00:18:16,300
Did you see that?

250
00:18:16,520 --> 00:18:17,660
Lord Odin!

251
00:18:18,060 --> 00:18:19,640
Has he finally returned?

252
00:18:20,140 --> 00:18:22,000
The true heir is back!

253
00:18:22,580 --> 00:18:24,345
Will he become the new Shogun?

254
00:18:25,500 --> 00:18:27,800
Odenshi's land will finally end!

255
00:18:30,840 --> 00:18:32,980
Shogun, you must evacuate!

256
00:18:33,520 --> 00:18:34,440
Excuse me?

257
00:18:34,680 --> 00:18:36,380
And why would I do that?

258
00:18:36,780 --> 00:18:39,200
Kozuki Oden has invaded the castle!

259
00:18:53,360 --> 00:18:54,900
Oden, let's talk!

260
00:18:55,140 --> 00:18:56,137
Don't hurt me!

261
00:18:56,220 --> 00:18:57,640
Careful now!

262
00:18:57,980 --> 00:19:01,392
If you lay one finger on me,
Kaido's not going to like it!

263
00:19:02,660 --> 00:19:06,601
Please think about what will happen
to this country if you kill me!

264
00:19:06,820 --> 00:19:09,620
I will, after I slice you.

265
00:19:13,300 --> 00:19:14,297
Oh no!

266
00:19:14,380 --> 00:19:15,240
I forgot!

267
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:22,100
This man's crazy!

268
00:19:29,400 --> 00:19:30,230
Orochie!

269
00:19:30,940 --> 00:19:32,740
Please don't do it, no!

270
00:19:58,160 --> 00:19:59,540
What the hell?

271
00:19:59,980 --> 00:20:01,780
Something stands in my way!

272
00:20:03,580 --> 00:20:04,560
A glass shield?

273
00:20:04,840 --> 00:20:05,820
It won't break!

274
00:20:09,560 --> 00:20:12,120
Stop hiding, Orochi!

275
00:20:14,500 --> 00:20:16,260
No, you coward!

276
00:20:19,940 --> 00:20:22,640
Be not afraid of your sake.

277
00:20:22,900 --> 00:20:24,040
I'll protect you.

278
00:20:24,860 --> 00:20:25,690
Hmm.

279
00:20:25,773 --> 00:20:28,504
Have some faith in my
barrier barrier technique.

280
00:20:32,260 --> 00:20:36,460
Anything attempting to breach this
area will be repelled, my lord.

281
00:20:36,860 --> 00:20:40,060
Your strength can do
nothing this time, Odin.

282
00:20:41,820 --> 00:20:43,460
Don't look so shocked.

283
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:47,537
I thought you would be more familiar with
this sort of thing since you're a pirate.

284
00:20:47,620 --> 00:20:51,855
Have you not witnessed the superhuman
abilities granted by Devil Fruits?

285
00:20:55,540 --> 00:20:58,200
You're a power user? That's correct.

286
00:20:58,480 --> 00:21:01,304
Although in this country
people call it sorcery.

287
00:21:02,300 --> 00:21:03,300
You fool!

288
00:21:03,540 --> 00:21:05,397
If anger and violence were the answer,

289
00:21:05,480 --> 00:21:08,137
your little daimyos would
have killed me already!

290
00:21:08,220 --> 00:21:09,520
It's too late for you!

291
00:21:09,840 --> 00:21:11,520
I'm untouchable!

292
00:21:19,460 --> 00:21:20,660
Face me!

293
00:21:22,580 --> 00:21:25,320
I don't understand how
this farce came to be.

294
00:21:25,560 --> 00:21:29,619
All I know is that my father pushed
for you to be the Shogun's proxy.

295
00:21:29,860 --> 00:21:31,840
But only until my return.

296
00:21:34,100 --> 00:21:37,512
I demand that you surrender
the Shogun's seat immediately.

297
00:21:37,780 --> 00:21:40,898
I never had any intention
of being the man in charge.

298
00:21:41,120 --> 00:21:44,660
However, I can still do better
for this country than you.

299
00:21:49,620 --> 00:21:51,160
Well, that's too bad.

300
00:21:51,640 --> 00:21:55,700
Seems you didn't hear what
Sukiyaki told us before he died.

301
00:21:56,900 --> 00:21:58,740
And what might that be?

302
00:22:03,940 --> 00:22:04,770
Hello.

303
00:22:04,853 --> 00:22:07,020
It's good to have you back, my son.

304
00:22:08,460 --> 00:22:09,290
Impossible.

305
00:22:09,373 --> 00:22:10,260
How are you alive?

306
00:22:13,740 --> 00:22:17,380
Your foolish daimyos were
deceived by the same trick!

307
00:22:19,060 --> 00:22:20,360
It was me!

308
00:22:21,820 --> 00:22:26,760
They fell for this hag in disguise thanks
to the power of the Clone Clone Fruits!

309
00:22:28,520 --> 00:22:31,280
The entire country bought
it for that matter!

310
00:22:32,040 --> 00:22:34,940
They let me take the
Shogun's Throne! Get it?

311
00:22:35,320 --> 00:22:38,520
I have no obligation to
give the position to you!

312
00:22:39,240 --> 00:22:40,260
At this point,

313
00:22:40,440 --> 00:22:45,028
nobody can possibly know what the real
Tsukiyaki was thinking on his deathbed!

314
00:22:45,700 --> 00:22:47,876
Pastor, what did you do to my father?

315
00:22:48,100 --> 00:22:50,420
Did he pass from illness or was it you?

316
00:23:10,100 --> 00:23:14,924
As the crowds looked up at the castle,
cheering for the return of the Kozuki clan,

317
00:23:15,140 --> 00:23:18,669
poisoned arrows rained down on
them, seemingly from nowhere.

318
00:23:19,040 --> 00:23:21,158
Two were injured, spitting up blood.

319
00:23:21,300 --> 00:23:22,600
They both fell blind.

320
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:25,882
The confused townspeople
could only take shelter.

321
00:23:28,720 --> 00:23:29,550
Suddenly,

322
00:23:29,633 --> 00:23:34,071
they witnessed an enormous dragon appear
in the darkened sky of the capital.

323
00:23:40,920 --> 00:23:44,720
Odin grew from a wild
child to a daimyo of Carol,

324
00:23:45,060 --> 00:23:48,942
then went to sea and journeyed
among the world's greatest pirates.

325
00:23:54,940 --> 00:23:59,780
He returned home many times stronger than
when he disembarked on his adventure.

326
00:24:00,980 --> 00:24:03,500
He was a man thought to be invincible.

327
00:24:05,400 --> 00:24:09,280
Don't you worry, if anyone,
Lord Odin will save our country.

328
00:24:11,000 --> 00:24:12,180
That's him there!

329
00:24:12,420 --> 00:24:13,361
You've returned!

330
00:24:13,700 --> 00:24:15,112
We were waiting for you!

331
00:24:15,200 --> 00:24:16,060
Lord Odin!

332
00:24:16,700 --> 00:24:19,717
The people of Wano saw him as a savior who

333
00:24:19,800 --> 00:24:22,329
could liberate them
from a ruthless tyrant.

334
00:24:24,920 --> 00:24:26,300
Is he okay?

335
00:24:26,800 --> 00:24:31,817
Within hours of his return, Kozugi
Odin stripped down to his loincloth.

336
00:24:31,900 --> 00:24:33,920
Outside of Shogun Orochi's palace.

337
00:24:35,740 --> 00:24:38,180
and danced like a fool.

338
00:24:40,500 --> 00:24:43,840
Orochi and Kaido's
underlings laughed at him.

339
00:24:48,940 --> 00:24:52,397
One, two, three...

340
00:24:52,480 --> 00:24:57,800
The once noble man danced and begged
for spare change, then marched away.

341
00:25:02,860 --> 00:25:07,154
What was supposed to be a momentous
occasion had become a disappointment.

342
00:25:07,340 --> 00:25:09,857
Kozuki Odin, the rightful
heir to the country.

343
00:25:09,940 --> 00:25:14,017
And the man who became their last hope
had turned into a complete laughingstock.

344
00:25:14,100 --> 00:25:15,380
to the entire nation.

345
00:25:16,580 --> 00:25:20,780
And soon, their frustration and
confusion gave way to anger.

346
00:25:24,040 --> 00:25:27,920
The foolish Odin has
hand-takes that amuse.

347
00:25:28,200 --> 00:25:31,660
His fear of snakes has
given him the blues.

348
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:35,480
And if you laugh with him, you will...

349
00:25:36,420 --> 00:25:39,040
Oden appeared in the capital once a week.

350
00:25:39,960 --> 00:25:43,666
He cambered about in front of
Orichy's castle seeking handouts.

351
00:25:44,540 --> 00:25:46,240
In pouring rain,

352
00:25:47,140 --> 00:25:48,580
gale-force winds

353
00:25:49,380 --> 00:25:51,260
and freezing snow.

354
00:25:57,160 --> 00:25:59,240
We are begging you, Lord Odin.

355
00:25:59,520 --> 00:26:00,740
Tell us the truth.

356
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:02,020
It's all we ask.

357
00:26:02,320 --> 00:26:04,880
What did you gonna
speak about with Orochi?

358
00:26:05,100 --> 00:26:05,960
Why do this?

359
00:26:06,160 --> 00:26:09,748
You've lost the support of even
your most faithful followers.

360
00:26:09,860 --> 00:26:12,154
Everyone's grown tired of this charade.

361
00:26:12,260 --> 00:26:15,260
I choose to dance in the
buff every week as my job.

362
00:26:15,480 --> 00:26:17,340
That's how I support my family!

363
00:26:18,760 --> 00:26:22,100
Word of his attics in the
capital reached Carol, too.

364
00:26:31,740 --> 00:26:37,180
Oh, don't forget one last thing,
the shirataki noodles, not bad.

365
00:26:38,220 --> 00:26:41,937
Whatever you do when you grow up,
don't be spineless like Lord Odin.

366
00:26:42,020 --> 00:26:44,597
You think real samurai
would act as a lapdog?

367
00:26:44,680 --> 00:26:46,660
They would sooner commit seppuku.

368
00:26:47,320 --> 00:26:50,997
Health is good for you,
better put it in the stew.

369
00:26:51,080 --> 00:26:54,820
Perfect stock and perfect
broth, brewing up for you!

370
00:27:01,700 --> 00:27:04,440
Then, a year later...

371
00:27:11,180 --> 00:27:16,300
Oden read the newspaper he received
from abroad, courtesy of Shogun Orochi.

372
00:27:28,120 --> 00:27:30,360
He ran up and down the coast.

373
00:27:30,600 --> 00:27:35,440
He couldn't help himself from wailing,
then laughing, then wailing again.

374
00:27:41,840 --> 00:27:43,460
Oh, Roger!

375
00:27:53,860 --> 00:27:56,200
24 years before the present day,

376
00:27:56,460 --> 00:28:01,048
the world was abuzz over the execution
of Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates.

377
00:28:01,820 --> 00:28:04,657
The allure of the vast
fortune he left behind

378
00:28:04,740 --> 00:28:07,505
encouraged countless
people to take to the sea,

379
00:28:07,680 --> 00:28:11,777
all of them hoping to traverse the Grand
Line and obtain the legendary treasure,

380
00:28:11,860 --> 00:28:12,780
the One Piece.

381
00:28:14,000 --> 00:28:17,360
This was the beginning
of the Great Pirate Era.

382
00:28:21,760 --> 00:28:23,160
ROAR!

383
00:28:32,620 --> 00:28:34,020
ROGER!

384
00:28:38,080 --> 00:28:40,020
An unbelievable life.

385
00:28:45,080 --> 00:28:47,340
What a remarkable man!

386
00:28:54,140 --> 00:28:57,857
It is now the second year since
Oden has returned from his voyage,

387
00:28:57,940 --> 00:28:59,917
and a mighty clash has broken out in Ringo

388
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:02,920
between the Gecko Pirates
and the Beast Pirates.

389
00:29:03,880 --> 00:29:06,700
Gecko Moria and Kaido go head-to-head.

390
00:29:14,560 --> 00:29:17,560
While the battle rages
on, a crime is committed.

391
00:29:17,880 --> 00:29:21,520
The grave of Ryuma is
ransacked, and Shusui is taken.

392
00:29:21,880 --> 00:29:24,720
Unfortunately, our hero is preoccupied.

393
00:29:25,320 --> 00:29:26,760
Radish and Frenchhold!

394
00:29:27,840 --> 00:29:29,920
Despite the chaos in his country,

395
00:29:30,220 --> 00:29:33,157
Oden faithfully dances in
the flower capital each week.

396
00:29:33,240 --> 00:29:35,517
I want to play! You're that man.

397
00:29:35,600 --> 00:29:39,157
Perfect chunk and perfect
broth brewing up for you.

398
00:29:39,240 --> 00:29:41,700
Odin wouldn't be Odin.

399
00:29:42,680 --> 00:29:44,940
If it wasn't boiled.

400
00:29:47,000 --> 00:29:49,217
The dullard is in the streets again.

401
00:29:49,300 --> 00:29:51,617
My heart is heavy for the people of Kuri.

402
00:29:51,700 --> 00:29:53,840
The foolish lord, huh?

403
00:29:55,240 --> 00:29:58,120
Hmm, bit of a stretch
to even call him a lord

404
00:29:59,620 --> 00:30:01,400
Stop running, Kiyoti!

405
00:30:01,920 --> 00:30:02,750
No!

406
00:30:02,833 --> 00:30:03,663
It's the way!

407
00:30:05,140 --> 00:30:08,611
I've turned my family into the
laughing stock of the nation

408
00:30:09,400 --> 00:30:10,230
Father!

409
00:30:11,900 --> 00:30:14,600
I love watching you so, so much!

410
00:30:14,740 --> 00:30:16,580
I want to see you do it, too!

411
00:30:19,720 --> 00:30:21,620
Hey, Toki Yes?

412
00:30:22,140 --> 00:30:23,600
Do you wish to leave me?

413
00:30:23,840 --> 00:30:25,437
Are you saying that in jest?

414
00:30:25,520 --> 00:30:26,640
You'd better be.

415
00:30:28,140 --> 00:30:32,137
Odin became known as the foolish
lord of Kuri throughout the country.

416
00:30:32,220 --> 00:30:35,897
The only people still willing to
associate with him were his family,

417
00:30:35,980 --> 00:30:38,437
his retainers, and a
handful of supporters.

418
00:30:38,520 --> 00:30:40,108
Are you certain about this?

419
00:30:40,380 --> 00:30:43,140
You all still wish to
serve as my retainers?

420
00:30:43,420 --> 00:30:46,600
Really think we have someplace
better to be? My lord,

421
00:30:46,720 --> 00:30:50,157
have you forgotten that we've been
acquainted with your naked dancing for years?

422
00:30:50,240 --> 00:30:51,070
No kidding.

423
00:30:51,153 --> 00:30:52,787
This is nothing you know us.

424
00:30:56,980 --> 00:30:57,810
Huh?

425
00:30:57,893 --> 00:30:59,997
Just what do you want
with Boss Hyogoro, huh?

426
00:31:00,080 --> 00:31:01,020
Back it up.

427
00:31:01,280 --> 00:31:04,580
I'd keep a good distance
if I were you. Stop it!

428
00:31:06,280 --> 00:31:07,110
Ouch!

429
00:31:07,480 --> 00:31:10,600
That's not your call to
make. Stand back! As you say.

430
00:31:11,060 --> 00:31:12,200
Sorry, ma 'am.

431
00:31:12,360 --> 00:31:13,478
Greetings, m 'lady.

432
00:31:13,580 --> 00:31:15,040
I apologize for them.

433
00:31:15,300 --> 00:31:17,300
Why not come in and have some tea?

434
00:31:18,260 --> 00:31:20,040
Oh, yo! Odin's here.

435
00:31:22,900 --> 00:31:25,740
That damned auto-chi just
won't leave me alone.

436
00:31:25,960 --> 00:31:28,078
I'd never work for someone like him.

437
00:31:30,480 --> 00:31:33,421
Well, don't put yourself
in danger, all right, yo?

438
00:31:33,680 --> 00:31:35,209
It's funny you stopped by.

439
00:31:35,340 --> 00:31:39,157
I was telling him the other day,
your dancing's gotten so much better.

440
00:31:39,240 --> 00:31:41,122
Stop it, you're making me blush.

441
00:31:44,080 --> 00:31:45,540
Anyway, another cup?

442
00:31:46,980 --> 00:31:48,700
Three years pass.

443
00:31:55,160 --> 00:31:57,513
He's back, still dancing in the streets.

444
00:31:57,700 --> 00:31:59,557
He's certainly devoted to this nonsense.

445
00:31:59,640 --> 00:32:01,875
...instilling it in the freezing cold.

446
00:32:03,720 --> 00:32:05,720
It's getting a bit nippy out here.

447
00:32:06,200 --> 00:32:07,380
Has he no shave?

448
00:32:07,580 --> 00:32:08,697
He is deranged.

449
00:32:08,780 --> 00:32:10,640
How obnoxious. Go away.

450
00:32:11,440 --> 00:32:15,420
Four years pass, and nothing in
the land of Wano has changed.

451
00:32:17,240 --> 00:32:21,040
Then in the fifth year,
Orochi makes a move on Kuri.

452
00:32:24,660 --> 00:32:25,820
It's the Shogun!

453
00:32:25,940 --> 00:32:27,240
What's he doing here?

454
00:32:51,380 --> 00:32:52,210
Shogun.

455
00:32:53,340 --> 00:32:55,360
It's been quite a while, Odin.

456
00:32:55,780 --> 00:32:56,610
Hasn't it?

457
00:32:56,693 --> 00:33:00,340
I found the location for
my next weapons factory.

458
00:33:00,740 --> 00:33:02,260
This'll do just fine.

459
00:33:02,780 --> 00:33:04,700
Oh, Odin, you do great work.

460
00:33:05,420 --> 00:33:06,460
Come on.

461
00:33:06,800 --> 00:33:08,120
Sorgan, a moment.

462
00:33:08,400 --> 00:33:09,777
You're forgetting something.

463
00:33:09,860 --> 00:33:12,742
What about the ship you
and Kaido promised him...

464
00:33:13,800 --> 00:33:15,620
What are you babbling about?

465
00:33:19,900 --> 00:33:21,960
Let's go back to the factory talk.

466
00:33:22,200 --> 00:33:26,141
They need to run effectively, so
I will need the strongest workers.

467
00:33:26,640 --> 00:33:29,397
I'm sure that the people of
Kuri won't disappoint me.

468
00:33:29,480 --> 00:33:30,400
Will they?

469
00:33:32,900 --> 00:33:34,440
Now get to work.

470
00:33:35,100 --> 00:33:38,806
Our country will be the greatest
weapons producer in the world.

471
00:33:43,640 --> 00:33:44,470
Orochi!

472
00:33:45,220 --> 00:33:46,660
I'm back of you!

473
00:33:47,420 --> 00:33:48,250
Aye, yes.

474
00:33:49,040 --> 00:33:51,360
By the way, Hyogoro became a problem.

475
00:33:51,700 --> 00:33:53,524
I had to call in a little help.

476
00:33:54,260 --> 00:33:55,848
Kaido's taking care of him.

477
00:33:58,660 --> 00:34:01,097
It's not like I didn't want
to work with the old man,

478
00:34:01,180 --> 00:34:03,827
but I grew tired of his
countless rejections.

479
00:34:04,780 --> 00:34:07,780
Such a pity he'll wind up dead. Dork!

480
00:34:08,340 --> 00:34:11,037
His underlings did put
up quite a fight, though.

481
00:34:11,120 --> 00:34:13,400
You unhand our boss right now!

482
00:34:15,520 --> 00:34:17,817
It's a shame we had to put them all down.

483
00:34:17,900 --> 00:34:20,018
Oops, they'd have made fine workers.

484
00:34:21,640 --> 00:34:25,577
It's funny thinking back on it, but
even his old lady tried to fend us off.

485
00:34:25,660 --> 00:34:29,577
She might have been a firecracker, but
what did she think she was gonna do?

486
00:34:29,660 --> 00:34:31,560
We shot her dead, of course

487
00:34:33,340 --> 00:34:34,170
No!

488
00:34:34,253 --> 00:34:35,380
I'll do anything!

489
00:34:36,100 --> 00:34:37,940
Don't take him away from me!

490
00:34:49,320 --> 00:34:53,140
You figure the wife of a Yakuza
boss would have more composure

491
00:34:56,300 --> 00:34:58,200
Anyway, how are your kids?

492
00:34:59,400 --> 00:35:00,820
Momonosuke and Hiyori?

493
00:35:01,360 --> 00:35:03,280
Getting big now, aren't they?

494
00:35:03,640 --> 00:35:06,020
They really grow up so fast.

495
00:35:06,260 --> 00:35:10,200
Quite a cute little pair of
children you've raised, I'm sure.

496
00:35:10,620 --> 00:35:12,180
I take good care of them.

497
00:35:15,620 --> 00:35:19,040
I expect to see progress on
that factory when I get back!

498
00:35:44,120 --> 00:35:45,000
That day,

499
00:35:45,240 --> 00:35:48,977
it became clear that the concerns of his
family and retainers were well-founded.

500
00:35:49,060 --> 00:35:54,300
The great samurai had been carrying a
terrible burden all alone for five long years.

501
00:36:04,360 --> 00:36:08,277
Curse you, Orochi, and Kaido.

502
00:36:08,360 --> 00:36:09,880
The time is now.

503
00:36:16,260 --> 00:36:17,717
You have our support.

504
00:36:17,800 --> 00:36:20,580
We've waited years to
hear you say those words.

505
00:36:25,040 --> 00:36:30,160
We'll aim for Kaido's island, wait for
him to drink until he loses consciousness,

506
00:36:30,660 --> 00:36:32,520
and cut off his head!

507
00:36:36,020 --> 00:36:37,220
Now bear witness.

508
00:36:41,740 --> 00:36:44,117
This is the tale of
Kozuki Odin's uprising,

509
00:36:44,200 --> 00:36:47,553
a tale of courage and tragedy
for which all of Wano wept.

510
00:36:48,060 --> 00:36:51,500
With him stood the nine
men he shaped into samurai.

511
00:36:52,240 --> 00:36:54,300
It began at twilight.

512
00:36:54,760 --> 00:36:57,817
The sun was a fierce red as
it warmed the backs of the

513
00:36:57,900 --> 00:37:00,897
loyal heroes marching towards
a long overdue battle.

514
00:37:00,980 --> 00:37:05,568
Even the blades at their waist seemed
eager to settle things once and for all.

515
00:37:07,440 --> 00:37:10,880
They were later honored
with the moniker Akazayo-9,

516
00:37:11,160 --> 00:37:15,637
or Red Scabbards, referring to their
blades painted crimson by the shedding sun.

517
00:37:15,720 --> 00:37:17,760
I can't jump higher than me!

518
00:37:17,940 --> 00:37:18,800
I can't!

519
00:37:25,260 --> 00:37:28,600
Their sole objective was
to slay the mighty Kaido.

520
00:37:28,900 --> 00:37:32,377
But the stirring tale of their
march is but a cherished memory.

521
00:37:32,460 --> 00:37:36,580
For this story ends tragically
with the execution of Kozuki Odin.

522
00:37:44,760 --> 00:37:48,677
The renowned series of events
that are about to unfold will be

523
00:37:48,760 --> 00:37:53,360
told for generations to come and
be known as the Hour of Legends.
